43:`just test-checker-lane` builds into `target/release` of the current checkout and reads the binary from there, so run it without `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` set.
53:- **Grammar sweep:** list every syntax or type form the code can receive and show each is handled or declined. Prefer a generated test over the grammar with the TypeScript checker as the oracle (`crates/semantic/tests/`) to a hand-picked list. Cover lone surrogates, computed keys, shadowing, `declare`, overloads and re-exports.
56:- **Output-preserving change:** diff `extract --json --quiet --no-cache` against a build of `main` on a large project and on Chakra, with `stats` removed. For resolver or checker changes, also compare peak memory and time with `just bench`, because a size regression can pass every test.
57:- **A request to the checker:** a test that each parameter you send changes the answer. `tsrs` ignores keys it does not know, so a misspelled field compiles and passes (`file` for `files` made every cold run type-check the whole program).
58:- **Measuring:** interleave the builds and compare CPU time as well as wall time. Drop any run that carries a checker fallback diagnostic: a timed-out request falls back to the structural answer, so that run's output differs. Benchmark a combination of changes together; estimates measured separately do not add.
